

# --- Subject -----------------------------------------------------------------
# One present-tense sentence that says what the change does.
# Start with a capital. No full stop at the end.
# No type prefix. "Add the frame loader", not "feat: add the frame loader".
# No version number. A commit does not change the version.
# Keep it short. The longest subject in MiruScriptX is 77 characters.
#
# --- Body --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave one blank line after the subject.
# Wrap at 80 columns.
# Say what was wrong, what the change does, and how you proved it.
# Name the evidence. A number you can show beats a word like "better".
#
# --- Rules -------------------------------------------------------------------
# One commit does one change.
# Code and its tests go in one commit. Documentation goes in its own.
# A rename across many files goes in a commit of its own, with no behaviour
# change in it.
# Write in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English. Short sentences, active
# voice, present tense.
# No em-dash. No emoji.
# No agent name, no Co-Authored-By line, no session link. A human writes this.
